  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Karamoja Resilience Support Unit II (KRSU II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  The goal of the Karamoja Resilience Support Unit-II (KRSU II) activity is to support the Government of Uganda (GOU) to plan and coordinate development projects in the Karamoja region to increase the effectiveness and efficiency of development assistance. With FY 2022 funds, KRSU II will analyze existing studies and strategies; conduct assessments on emerging development challenges and opportunities in Karamoja; and disseminate new evidence from studies focused on agriculture, natural resource management, and nutrition-related social behavior changes, amongst others, to the GOU, donors, partners, USAID, and other stakeholders to inform and guide improved development planning and service delivery in the Karamoja sub-region.KRSU II will facilitate coordination of the GOU, development partners, and agencies providing humanitarian assistance in Karamoja to network, and identify areas for collective action. KRSU will continue to provide organizational and technical support for coordination structures, such as the Health and Nutrition and Social Behavior Change working groups, amongst others. KRSU II will also assist the GOU&apos;s Ministry for Karamoja Affairs to better coordinate with district and sub-county leadership to operationalize the Karamoja Integrated Development Plan, guide investments, and share development results.  KRSU II will enhance the GOU&apos;s coordination capacity to eventually assume the role in the future..</narrative>
  </description>
